From: Press5elect <press5elect@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] radv: threaded recording: the worker reads the clock once in 64 pauses

The worker's look for more work read the clock at every pause. A clock read is a
call, and on the PS5 the title answers it from the processor's counter under a
compare-and-swap on a line that every thread's clock reads share, so the worker's
loop kept that line bouncing between cores and slowed the threads that render and
emulate (Crux2's profile of the worker on the console, 2026-10-21: 46% of its time
inside clock reads). The clock is now read once in 64 pauses; the 50 us it looks for
work are the same.

SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Press5elect
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
---
diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/layers/radv_threaded_layer.c b/src/amd/vulkan/layers/radv_threaded_layer.c
index 23f43ded0e8..d2198e4b7de 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/layers/radv_threaded_layer.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/layers/radv_threaded_layer.c
@@ -40,6 +40,8 @@
 #define RADV_THREADED_MAX_COMMANDS 512
 /* How long the worker looks for more work before it sleeps. */
 #define RADV_THREADED_SPIN_NS 50000
+/* Pauses between two reads of the clock while it looks (about 64 x 40 ns on a Zen 2). */
+#define RADV_THREADED_SPIN_CHECK 64
 
 struct radv_threaded_batch {
    struct list_head link;
@@ -110,9 +112,20 @@ radv_threaded_worker(void *opaque)
          /* Look for more for a while before sleeping: the application's thread
           * hands over batches every few draws and waking a sleeper costs it. */
          mtx_unlock(&rec->lock);
+         /* The clock is read once in RADV_THREADED_SPIN_CHECK pauses: a read is a call
+          * and, on the PS5, a compare-and-swap on a line every thread's clock reads
+          * share, so a loop reading it at every pause slowed the threads that render
+          * and emulate (Crux2's profile of the worker: half its time in the clock). */
          const uint64_t until = radv_threaded_now_ns() + RADV_THREADED_SPIN_NS;
-         while (!p_atomic_read(&rec->queued) && radv_threaded_now_ns() < until)
+         unsigned pauses = 0;
+         while (!p_atomic_read(&rec->queued)) {
             __builtin_ia32_pause();
+            if (++pauses == RADV_THREADED_SPIN_CHECK) {
+               pauses = 0;
+               if (radv_threaded_now_ns() >= until)
+                  break;
+            }
+         }
          mtx_lock(&rec->lock);
 
          if (list_is_empty(&rec->batches) && !rec->stop) {
